{% extends "base.jinja" %}
{% block title %}
  {{ super() }} | {{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-title") }}
{% endblock title %}
{% block content %}
  {# Where a browser is left after signing in on an app's behalf
     (src/handoff.rs). Nothing was signed in here: this window carried what
     the provider said back to the app, which is going on by itself.

     So the one thing left is to put the app back in front, which it cannot
     do for itself from here -- a tab the browser opened is not one a script
     may close. `oeee-cafe://handoff/done` is what does it: being opened is
     all the apps use the scheme for, and they load nothing from it
     (AndroidManifest.xml in oeee-cafe-android, handoff.rs in
     oeee-cafe-desktop, the callback scheme of ASWebAuthenticationSession in
     oeee-cafe-apple). It carries nothing; the app is already holding the
     secret that claims the sign-in.

     The link is here to be pressed as well as followed by itself. A browser
     may refuse to leave for another application without somebody asking it
     to, and whoever reached this page in an ordinary browser -- with no app
     waiting -- has something to read instead of an error. #}
  <div class="auth-page">
    <div class="ds-card auth-card">
      <h1 class="auth-title">{{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-title") }}</h1>
      <p class="auth-lede">{{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-body") }}</p>
      <a class="ds-button ds-button-primary auth-submit"
         href="oeee-cafe://handoff/done">{{ ftl_get_message("handoff-done-return") }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script>
    // Once, and with replace, so going back does not land here again.
    try {
      location.replace("oeee-cafe://handoff/done");
    } catch (error) {
      // No app to take it: the page above says what to do instead.
    }
  </script>
{% endblock content %}
